                "licensed_as": "NEWPORT ACADEMY - HAPPY VALLEY",
                "findings": [
                    {
                        "text": "LPA found that in January-February 2026 clients continually found contraband near the facility, and though some measures such as increased body/room searches were put in place, preventative measures were not implemented despite management being made aware of the issue of contraband being left near the premises -- leading to clients continuing to obtain contraband. LPA issued one Type A deficiency under CCR 84072(d)(1) Personal Rights.See attached LIC9099-D. The preponderance of evidence standard has been met, and therefore the above allegations are found to be substantiated. An exit interview was conducted, appeal rights were discussed, and a copy of this report was emailed to Crystal Butler, Compliance Manager. This document is sent for digital signature. An exit interview was conducted and a copy of this report was emailed to Crystal Butler, Compliance Manager. This document is sent for digital signature.",
                        "standard": "84072(d)(1)",
                        "label": "Substantiated"
                    }
                ]
            },
